1
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:38,500
Keeping secrets, are ye?

2
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:11,000
The Lighthouse is a drama, fantasy, thriller film directed by Robert Eggers.

3
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:43,500
Two lighthouse keepers try to maintain their sanity while living on a
remote and mysterious New England island in the 1890s.

4
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Thomas Howard, played by Robert Pattinson.

5
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:48,500
Thomas Wake, played by Willem Dafoe.

6
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:21,000
Mermaid, played by Valeriia Karaman.

7
00:31:47,500 --> 00:31:53,500
Ephraim Winslow, played by Logan Hawkes.

8
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:26,000
Woman on the Rocks, played by Kyla Nicolle.

9
00:40:52,500 --> 00:40:58,500
Departing Wickie, played by Shaun Clarke.

10
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:31,000
The Lighthouse is a 2019 film directed and produced by Robert Eggers,
from a screenplay cowritten with his brother Max Eggers.

11
00:49:57,500 --> 00:50:03,500
It stars Willem Dafoe and Robert Pattinson as turmoiled nineteenth-century lighthouse
keepers stranded at a remote New England outpost by a violent storm.

12
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:36,000
The film has defied genre categorization in media, leading
to multiple interpretations from critics.

13
00:59:02,500 --> 00:59:08,500
The idea of The Lighthouse first emerged from Max Eggers's re-envisioning of
Edgar Allan Poe's unfinished short story of the same name.

14
01:03:35,000 --> 01:03:41,000
Robert Eggers assisted the development when Max was unable to complete his adaptation, sourcing
the plot from a nineteenth-century legend of an accident at a Welsh lighthouse.

15
01:08:07,500 --> 01:08:13,500
The Lighthouse draws visually from photography of 1890s New England,
maritime-themed French cinema from the 1930s, and symbolist art.

16
01:12:40,000 --> 01:12:46,000
Principal photography took place in Nova Scotia, Canada, beginning
in April 2018 and lasting slightly over a month.

17
01:17:12,500 --> 01:17:18,500
It was shot in black-and-white, with a nearly-square 1.19:1 aspect ratio.

18
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:51,000
Mark Korven developed the film's score, evoking the
sounds and mythologies of the sea.

19
01:26:17,500 --> 01:26:23,500
The film premiered at the Cannes Film Festival on May 19, 2019, and was
theatrically released in the United States by A24 on October 18, 2019.

20
01:30:50,000 --> 01:30:56,000
It grossed over $18 million, against an $11 million budget, and received widespread critical acclaim,
with particular praise for the direction, visuals, and performances of Dafoe and Pattinson.

21
01:35:22,500 --> 01:35:28,500
Among its numerous accolades, the film was nominated for Best Cinematography at
the 92nd Academy Awards and the 73rd British Academy Film Awards.

22
01:39:55,000 --> 01:40:01,000
The film explores themes of island, nightmare,
isolation, mermaid, hallucination.

23
01:44:27,500 --> 01:44:33,500
The tone is emotional and intense.
